# Transformer Patterns — project conventions

## Project identity

This is **Transformer Patterns** (*UX flow patterns and lo-fi prototyping for
transformation teams*) — built with React 19, TypeScript, Vite 8, and React Flow.

### Two distinct artefacts

**Transformers Patterns** (core) — the P1–P10 interaction pattern inventory, UPL
shell model, and composition rules. These are the team's canonical definition of
how operator interfaces should behave and are structured. In production, patterns
are implemented using **Podium** (the high-fidelity design system).

**LOFI Kit** (tool) — a low-fidelity, grayscale, monospace component library
(`lib/`) for fast prototyping. It is used here to render live pattern examples.
It is **not** the production design system. Demos use LOFI Kit components to keep
prototypes abstract and focused on structure over visual polish.

Public UI exports use a **`LOFI` prefix** (e.g. `LOFIButton`, `LOFIModal`).
Diagram exports (`nodeTypes`, `edgeTypes`) are unprefixed.

**Default fidelity is Lo-fi** in this workspace. All prototypes use grayscale,
monospace typography, and `lofi-kit` components. Never ask the user to specify
"lo-fi" — it is always assumed.

---

## Hard rules (no exceptions)

- **No colour.** `#111` ink, `#fff` paper, token grays only. No colour ramp,
  no accent colours, no arbitrary hex values.
- **No external UI libraries in demos or app code** — **except** a **dedicated
  high-fidelity demo package** under `demos/<slug>/` that is created or maintained
  under the **`/high-fidelity`** Cursor skill workflow: that package **may** use
  **Podium** (and its documented Mantine stack) from npm. **All other** demos
  and demo UI code use **`lofi-kit` only**. No Radix, shadcn, MUI, or other UI
  frameworks in those paths. **`lib/`** never imports Podium or themed kits.
- **`lib/` may depend on headless, unstyled behavior primitives** (currently:
  `@radix-ui/react-collapsible`) **as an implementation detail only.** These
  are bundled into `lofi-kit` and are never part of the public design API.
  Still forbidden inside `lib/`: themed component kits, CSS-in-JS UI frameworks,
  Tailwind, colour.
- **No raw `<button>` or `<input>` in the UI layer.** Use `LOFIButton` and `LOFIInput`
  from `lofi-kit`.
- **No modal stacking by default.** A modal never opens another modal, with one exception: a **confirmation-only** overlay (P7 — title, message, two buttons, no forms or tables) may appear on top of a primary editor modal when a destructive or save action inside it requires confirmation. This is the only permitted stacking pattern. Any other stacking scenario requires explicit stakeholder approval before implementation.
- **No invented components.** If a pattern requires something `lofi-kit`
  does not have, flag it before writing code.
- **Monospace everywhere.** All text uses `$text-font-family`. Use the `LOFIText`
  component for all rendered copy.
- **BEM naming.** `.component-name`, `.component-name__element`,
  `.component-name--modifier`. No utility classes, no inline styles.
- **SCSS with tokens.** Always `@use '../../styles/tokens' as *;` in component
  stylesheets. Never hard-code colours or sizes.
- **Spacing grid.** All SCSS spacing uses `$space-*` tokens from the 4 / 8 px
  grid. Regular layout: `$space-4`–`$space-16` (8–32 px). Fine intra-component:
  `$space-2` / `$space-6` (4 / 12 px). Never hard-code arbitrary pixel values.

