## Compliance debt

Some files in `demos/bracket-demo/src/components/` still use raw HTML
(`<button>`, `<select>`, etc.) instead of `lofi-kit` components:

- `EdgeContextMenu.tsx`
- `ProgressionEdge.tsx` (edge label control)

When touching these files, migrate the UI elements you interact with to
their `lofi-kit` equivalents. Do not copy their raw HTML patterns into new
code. Reference `docs/LOFI_BLOCKS.md` → "Forbidden raw HTML" for the substitution
table.

---

## Key commands

```bash
npm run dev                  # Hub on :5172 + demos + Storybook
npm run dev:bracket-demo     # bracket-demo Vite only (no hub)
npm run build:lofi           # Build lofi-kit → lib/dist
npm run storybook    # Storybook on :6006
npm test             # Vitest
npm run lint         # ESLint
npm run format       # Prettier
```

---

## Agent instruction parity (Cursor + Copilot)

Canonical behaviour lives in **`docs/`** (especially `UX_PATTERNS*.md`, `UI_PATTERNS*.md`, `COMPOSITION_PATTERNS.md`, `NL_COMPONENT_MAPPING_LO_FI.md`, `NL_COMPONENT_MAPPING_HI_FI.md`). **GitHub Copilot** consumes `.github/copilot-instructions.md`. When you change pattern semantics or Cursor rules that mirror those docs, update **both** surfaces in one change-set unless you explicitly defer with a noted TODO. See `ux-patterns-copilot-parity.mdc`.

